{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791626730,"nonce":"Hdez9BvJtldA195SNCEapmdRuwQ=","title":"An interpreter-to-LLVM OSR entry decodes an f32 register as f32 bits","message":"The interpreter hands an HF32 register to an OSR entry as the f64 it widens to (value_to_i64 stores as_f64().to_bits(); HF32 registers are already rounded to f32 after every operation). The LLVM entry (compile_snapshot_entry, load_air_osr_slot in crates/ash/src/llvm/function/mod.rs) truncated the slot to i32 and bit-cast it to f32, so the register took the low bits of an f64 mantissa. The answer is wrong and nothing reports it.\n\nReproducer: a while loop that accumulates a Single in a function called once (crates/ash/test/tests/TestOsrF32.hx).\n\n    ash --mode interp                                          f32=382381.375\n    ash --mode hybrid --jit-tier llvm --jit-threshold 1        f32=103514.140625\n\nThe default ladder was protected only because the Cranelift OSR entry declined any function with an f32 register, so an LLVM entry was reached only through the promote-time batch of a function with an f32 register. The compiled-snapshot (re-tier) ABI is different: Cranelift's exit writes the f32's own bits, and that path was right.\n\nFound while chasing c695a38.","files":null}]}